  "question": "How do AMD and Apple differ regarding the finality of administrative decisions in their equity plans?",
  "answer": "AMD decisions are final and conclusive, while Apple states discretionary provisions do not create participant rights.",
  "quote_a": "any action taken or ruling or decision made, by the Plan Administrator... shall be final and conclusive as to all parties",
  "quote_b": "provisions of the Plan that confer discretionary authority on the Board or the Committee do not... create any rights in the Participant"
}
